  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1403.02 Structural Analysis and Design",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1403.02 Structural Analysis and Design.\n\n(a) In the event that designs are not available from a manufacturer or fabricator of a device, the operator shall furnish a structural analysis to the department. A structural analysis shall consist of a written statement by an individual designated by the department, qualified by skill and experience, to conduct an analysis of the carnival or amusement ride or associated electrical equipment.\n\n(b) For the purposes of this section, qualified by skill and experience means that the individual possesses a professional engineering degree in the specific area(s) being addressed by the design, and has completed an actual inspection while accompanied by an agent of the commissioner, to determine attention to detail, completeness of inspection, and proper procedure.\n\n(c) Designs of a device or a structural analysis shall be required for carnival or amusement rides that the agents are unfamiliar with.\n\n(d) Notwithstanding (b) above, challenge courses and zip lines shall be designed and approved in conformance with standards set forth in either the “ANSI/ACCT 03-2019 CHALLENGE COURSES AND CANOPY/ZIP LINE TOURS STANDARDS” (Revision of ANSI/ACCT 03-2016 Standards), or the ASTM International standards listed in Saf-C 1402.01(a), available as noted in Appendix B.\n\nSource. #2229, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2950, eff 1-3-85; ss by #4321, eff 10-6-87; ss by #4531, eff 1-1-89; ss by #5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95; ss by #5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\nNew. #7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\nNew. #8045, eff 2-20-04; amd by #8319, EMERGENCY, eff 4-5-05, EXPIRED: 10-2-05; amd by #8342, eff 4-28-05; ss by #8649, eff 6-2-06; ss by #10507, eff 1-21-14; amd by #12615, eff 8-28-18; ss by #13666, eff 6-20-23; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
